# Pentatonic Box 2 Lick (repertoire plan: st-pent-box-2). An original 8-bar study in A minor
# pentatonic box 2, frets 7 to 10, over a one-chord Am7 groove. Four 2-bar phrases in call and
# response: phrases 1 and 3 ask (they stop on G and on E, chord tones that leave the door open),
# phrases 2 and 4 answer (they come home to A: the low A on string 4, then the high A on string 2).
# All 12 notes of the box are used, and nothing else.
# One finger per fret, as the Scales screen shows the box: finger 1 on fret 7, finger 2 on fret 8,
# finger 3 on fret 9, finger 4 on fret 10.
# The slide opens the study: finger 3 plays D at string 3 fret 7 (where it sits in box 1) and
# slides up to E at fret 9, which carries the whole hand from box 1 into box 2.
title: Pentatonic Box 2 Lick
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original study in A minor pentatonic, box 2
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 5
tags: minor pentatonic, box 2, call and response, lick, slide
tempo: 88
time: 4/4
key: Am

